Sockets in the service's live folder

libpq and the server take /tmp for the folder of the Unix socket unless
told otherwise (DEFAULT_PGSOCKET_DIR). The service's socket is in its live
folder, /system/live/services/postgres, which Spark makes for the account
postgres and the service script opens to everyone; this makes that folder
the default of the server, libpq and so of psql and every program built
on libpq, which then find the service without -h, as Debian's find
/var/run/postgresql (its patch 51-default-sockets-in-var.patch). A server
run by hand, without the service, has no such folder: it is started with
-k or unix_socket_directories, and its clients are given PGHOST or -h.

diff --git a/src/include/pg_config_manual.h b/src/include/pg_config_manual.h
--- a/src/include/pg_config_manual.h
+++ b/src/include/pg_config_manual.h
@@ -195,7 +195,18 @@
  * support them yet.
  */
 #ifndef WIN32
+#ifdef __radix__
+/*
+ * The live folder of the service that runs the server.  It is where Spark
+ * makes a service's sockets, and it is the server's account's own: the
+ * service's script opens it to everyone, since the server authenticates each
+ * connection itself.  A server started by hand has no such folder and uses
+ * -k, unix_socket_directories or PGHOST.
+ */
+#define DEFAULT_PGSOCKET_DIR  "/system/live/services/postgres"
+#else
 #define DEFAULT_PGSOCKET_DIR  "/tmp"
+#endif
 #else
 #define DEFAULT_PGSOCKET_DIR ""
 #endif
